@startuml

participant "Client 1" as client1
participant "Server" as server
participant "Client 2" as client2

== Join the server ==

note right of client1
The socket is instanciated and the connection is
automatically etablished.
end note

client1->server : Establish connection
server<-->client1 : Connection established
server->client1 : INIT <height> <widht> <winLenght>

client2->server : Establish connection
server<-->client2 : Connection established
server->client2 : INIT <height> <widht> <winLenght>

note right of client1
The two client receive wich one start playing and wich
one start waiting. 
end note
server->client1 : PLAY
server->client2 : WAIT

== Loop Placing tokens ==

note right of client1
The gameboard is set to a 5x5 gameboard
(index available 0 to 4).
end note

client1->server : PLACE 0
server->client1 : TOKEN_PLACED
server->client2 : GAME_CONTINUE 
server->client2 : INSERTED 0

client2->server : PLACE 1
server->client2 : TOKEN_PLACED
server->client1 : GAME_CONTINUE
server->client1 : INSERTED 1

client1->server : PLACE 0
server->client1 : TOKEN_PLACED 
server->client2 : GAME_CONTINUE
server->client2 : INSERTED 0

== And so on, until ... ==

== Placing a winning token ==

note left of client2
Let's admit the Client 2 placed a token
and win.
end note

client2->server : PLACE 0
server->client2 : TOKEN_PLACED 
server->client1 : LOSE
server->client1 : INSERTED 0

server->client2 : WIN

== Quit the game ==

note right of client1
The server close the client connection when
the game finished.
end note

server->server : Remove Client 1 from players
client1<-->server : Connection closed

server->server : Remove Client 2 from players
client2<-->server : Connection closed



@enduml